    "text": "Research · Data and retrieval How data becomes reliable evidence A good answer needs a trustworthy record, a search method suited to the question and a path back to the source. TK Tony Koo 15 October 2026 · 3 min read Source-backed editorial synthesis Protect the record before optimizing search A database is more than a place to put rows. Keys and constraints can prevent impossible states, while transactions keep related changes together. PostgreSQL’s constraint documentation makes this concrete: a policy clause should carry a document ID, version, effective date and owner so a later answer can identify exactly which rule it used. Store the original file or immutable source reference alongside extracted text. For a question about a current policy, retrieval should filter by effective version and permissions before ranking text. A semantically similar but superseded clause is not evidence for today’s answer. Choose exact or approximate retrieval deliberately Use exact lookup for identifiers, dates and strict filters. Use lexical search when the user’s terms matter; vector search helps surface semantically related candidates. Faiss documents exact flat indexes and approximate options including HNSW. Approximate indexes trade some recall for speed or memory. They can narrow candidates, but a close vector is not proof that a passage answers the question. Figure. This RAG example separates ingestion from answer serving. Retrieval still needs version, permission, and provenance checks. Source: Google Cloud · RAG architecture · CC BY 4.0 . Worked example “What is the approval threshold for overseas travel?” first filters the current travel-policy version. Search returns two candidate clauses. The system quotes the relevant span, checks its effective date and cites the policy section; if versions conflict, it asks for review. Code navigation has the same first question—what evidence is current?—but its retrieval tools are different. Syntax trees, symbol indexes and language servers help locate definitions and references; the agent must still read the source and validate the patch. See how coding agents find and change code . Evaluate the path to an answer Measure retrieval recall on questions with known source spans, then evaluate whether the answer is supported by those spans. Keep query, retrieved IDs, rank, source versions and final citation in an inspectable trace. This lets you tell a retrieval miss from a reasoning error. The same design supports corrections when a document is replaced or access is revoked. Read the original sources PostgreSQL constraints Primary documentation on keys and integrity rules. Faiss index catalogue Exact and approximate index mechanisms, including HNSW. Google Cloud · RAG architecture Google Cloud architecture figure; converted from SVG to PNG. Read next: How to choose a system boundary In this story"
